@page "/framework/architecture"

<PageTitle>Architecture · louis-agent</PageTitle>
<PageHead Description="The whole louis-agent framework as its repository is laid out: every project that ships, by family, from the engine to the sites." />

<Band Id="top" Kicker="Architecture">
    <BandTitle Class="chrome">The whole framework, as the repository is laid out.</BandTitle>
    <p class="lede">Every project that ships has its place here, one line each. The folders say what ships: <code>src/</code> is the framework and its own site, <code>packs/</code> what an agent can do, <code>demos/</code> what someone built on it. A test holds this page to the solution file, so a new project can't be left off.</p>
    <pre class="listing"><code>src/engine/   the engine: core, and what sits on it, one library each
src/hosts/    the hosts, as libraries: a CLI, Rider's protocol, the HTTP API, the MCP server, the accounts
src/web/      the framework's web: what every site shares
src/evals/    the eval harness, its checks contract, its protocol and its runner
src/tools/    a developer's tools: the usage probe, the film export
src/site/     the framework's own website: this site, its guide and its host, built on the framework
packs/        tools/ (the packs), evals/ (what proves one), web/ (a pack's screens), tests/
demos/        louis-agent/ (the coding agent, its chat and admin), puls/ (the assistant), starter/ (the smallest site)
              each with identity/, hosts/, web/, evals/, config/, docker/, deploy/, tests/ and docs/</code></pre>
    <GraphView Spec="ArchitectureGraph.Spec" Title="The groups of the repository, and which rests on which" />
</Band>

